hings for navigating the creative life, released weekly as a part of </em><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\"><em>labyrinth library</em></a><em>. </em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n\n\n   \n    <a href=\"https://keningzhu.notion.site/infinity-lake-excerpt\" target=\"_blank\">\n      explore infinity lake\n    </a>\n    \n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  <p>this first artifact of season 2 of Labyrinth is for immersing us into the watery, intuitive realms of Pisces. the infinity lake is metaphorical place to soak yourself in imaginal worlds of the psyche, and see what you discover. <br /><br />I visited my infinity lake a few times, and found that on each visit, my infinity lake — and its surrounding landscapes — looked very different. in my last visit, the lake was black (but warm) and inside a dark, ice cave with shimmering crystals. <br /><br /><strong>Purpose</strong>: being in relationship with lunar waters. to actively engage with the hidden parts of your creative psyche as a tiny, ongoing practice. </p><p><strong>Guiding Question: </strong>what is present in my creative psyche, beneath my conscious awareness?<br /><strong><br />Astrological Season: </strong>Pisces<strong><br /><br /></strong><a href=\"https://keningzhu.notion.site/infinity-lake-excerpt\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Explore Infinity Lake</strong></a><strong> </strong><em>(listen to a 5 min excerpt)</em> </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p><strong>🦋 </strong>explore<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\"><strong>Labyrinth Library</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"fead6c299a289ede27dadf79c743e5f6a8314a63c62baa10d6cda184c589fa90","category":"Sites"}